From 6110d5ae893ecd919ce0301f367ab8e9e4f280cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexis Williams <alexis@typedr.at>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:35:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] spa: alsa: Fix external volume reads and writes

ReadVolume and ReadMute read their value from the wrong JSON iterator,
the varlink client stopped parsing before "continues", absolute volume
writes sent the previous volume, and a second write while one awaited
its reply failed. Writes are now oneway, volumes reported by the
service are clamped to the valid range, and the service connection is
set up once per card.

The varlink client now delivers every complete message in a read
instead of leaving later ones buffered until more data arrives, and
compacts its buffer so long-lived connections don't overflow it.
Reply callbacks may make new calls or destroy the client. Writes use
MSG_NOSIGNAL and never leave half a message on the socket: a write
that would block is dropped with -EAGAIN, and one cut short
disconnects. Sync calls send with MSG_DONTWAIT so a peer that stops
reading can't block the caller, and a sync call that times out or
fails disconnects, so a late reply can't be taken as the answer to
the next call. Connect failures report the real errno and log at
debug level, leaving it to callers how loudly to report them.

The client also refuses calls once disconnected instead of writing to
a closed fd, reads replies sent just before a hangup, honours
sync-call timeouts of a second or more, closes the socket when connect
fails, and frees destroyed clients, which impl_clear otherwise loops on
forever.

The external volume paths also wait for a port to be selected: the
service is addressed by route, and devices are enabled, and their
volume read, before any port is active.
